            <ArticleTitle>[Hemorrhage caused by anticoagulants as a manifestation of occult diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1269-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Of 950 patients submitted to anticoagulant treatment for various reasons, 38 presented a major haemorrhage. In 21, bleeding was due to at times serious diseased, including 7 previously undetected malignant tumours. Haemorrhage was certainly fostered by the treatment but the accident permitted recognition of the occult disease in advance, thus increasing cure chances. When non-traumatic haemorrhage occurs during anticoagulant treatment, depth research should always be carried out with a view to detecting occult disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
